# Line endings are a property of THIS REPOSITORY, not of one workstation's git
# config (app-blueprints BLUEPRINT §10). Anything a Linux host executes or
# parses must arrive with LF: a CRLF shebang fails as `\r: command not found`,
# and systemd refuses to parse a unit file with CRLF at all.
#
# These rules are here before the files are, because the failure they prevent
# appears at deploy time on a machine that is not this one.
#
# Deliberately targeted rather than `* text=auto` — a blanket rule renormalizes
# every tracked file at once, which buries real changes in a repo-wide diff.

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.timer     text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
